1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Every morning, Thomas made coffee for two.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,000
He'd set two mugs on the kitchen counter,

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
pour the rich brew, and place one gently in front

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
of the empty chair across from him.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
It had been a year since Lily passed.

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
They used to start each day sharing stories, dreams,

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
or just peaceful silence over steaming cups.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000
She loved hers with a hint of cinnamon.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Thomas never forgot.

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
One chilly morning, as he prepared the usual two cups,

11
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
his granddaughter Emma came to visit.

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
She watched him set the scene, puzzled, grandpa,

13
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
why do you still make two cups?

14
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
He smiled a little sadly,

15
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
because love doesn't leave when someone does.

16
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
She's still here in the quiet moments.

17
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Emma nodded and sat in Lily's chair, picking up the cup.

18
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Then maybe we can share this one together.

19
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Thomas' eyes welled up, but his heart felt warm again.

20
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,000
For the first time in a long while,

21
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
the silence wasn't so lonely.

22
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Sometimes, love stays in the little things,

23
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,000
like a cup of coffee never meant to be empty.

